menu "embpet tgbot"

    config EMBPET_TG_BRIDGE
        bool "Telegram bridge (tg send, poller, routing, pending table)"
        default y
        help
            Starts the tg_poll and tg_send tasks and registers the tg
            commands (README 2.1, 3.4). Only the Bot API client test build
            (tgtest.defaults) turns it off, because its own test workers
            poll the same bot and two getUpdates loops conflict (HTTP 409).

    config EMBPET_TG_TEST
        bool "Bot API client test commands (never enable in production)"
        default n
        help
            Compiles in test-only console commands (`tg t_*`): store a token,
            call getMe / deleteWebhook / getUpdates / sendMessage from two
            worker tasks that own the poll and send connections, and run a
            polling + sending soak with heap statistics. Used by
            tools/tg_test.py. With the bridge on it also adds the bridge test
            commands (owner chat, injected updates, pending entries, stack
            headroom) used by tools/bridge_test.py.

endmenu
